{% comment %}
  Renders the string "true" when a product is final sale, nothing otherwise.

  Final sale means no return and no exchange. The rule lives here alone so the
  product page, the add-to-cart property, and anything added later all agree.

  A product is final sale when ANY of these hold:
    1. It is on sale — any variant priced below its compare-at price.
    2. Its product type is in FINAL_SALE_TYPES below.
    3. It belongs to a collection in FINAL_SALE_COLLECTIONS below.
    4. It is tagged "final-sale" or "final sale".

  The tag "returnable" overrides everything and forces the product back to
  returnable. Use it for the one-off exception.

  To widen the rule, add to the two lists below — lowercase, comma-separated,
  no spaces around the commas. Nothing else needs to change.
    - Types come from the product's "Product type" field in the admin.
    - Collections are handles (the last part of the collection URL).

  Accepts:
  - product: {Object} Product Liquid object

  Usage — capture the render, then test it with `contains` so stray whitespace
  can never flip the result:
    {%- capture final_sale %}{% render 'final-sale', product: product %}{% endcapture -%}
    {%- if final_sale contains 'true' -%}
{% endcomment %}
{%- liquid
  assign final_sale_types = 'vintage,home decor'
  assign final_sale_collections = 'swimwear'

  assign tags = product.tags | join: ',' | downcase | prepend: ',' | append: ','
  assign is_final_sale = false

  unless tags contains ',returnable,'
    if product.compare_at_price_max > product.price_min
      assign is_final_sale = true
    endif

    if tags contains ',final-sale,' or tags contains ',final sale,'
      assign is_final_sale = true
    endif

    assign product_type = product.type | downcase
    assign type_list = final_sale_types | split: ','
    if product_type != blank and type_list contains product_type
      assign is_final_sale = true
    endif

    assign collection_list = final_sale_collections | split: ','
    for collection in product.collections
      if collection_list contains collection.handle
        assign is_final_sale = true
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endunless

  if is_final_sale
    echo 'true'
  endif
-%}
